 "intro_html": "A jeongol is cooked and served in a <b>wide, shallow pan</b> on the table, so a steel sauté pan is the right tool here, not a substitute. Several kinds of mushroom sit in neat sections over napa cabbage and onion, with tofu and an optional mound of seasoned minced beef in the centre. A clear, lightly salted soy broth goes around the edge. It is mild, light and ready in half an hour. Use <a href=\"niboshi-bonito-dashi.html\">niboshi dashi</a> or, for a vegetarian pot, <a href=\"shiitake-kombu-dashi.html\">shiitake-kombu dashi</a>. This is a home adaptation built from several Korean sources and has not been kitchen tested.",
