   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cut the napa cabbage into <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"4\" data-s=\"0\">4 cm</span> pieces. Cut the ends off the onion, halve it and slice it lengthwise, along the lines, about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"mm\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 mm</span> thick. Slice the carrot into thin rounds. Cut the tofu into <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 cm</span> thick slices and the spring onions into <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 cm</span> lengths.</li><li>If using beef, mix it with the soy sauce, 1 minced clove of garlic, sesame oil and pepper.</li><li>Stir the broth together: dashi, soy sauce, the other minced garlic clove and the fish sauce.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
